+# Captured fraction: **−776.278718%** (`−7.762787×`)
+
+Status: **`DIAGNOSTIC_NOT_CLAIM`**
+
+The occupancy-three floor captures none of the oracle's gain over unilateral.
+Its pooled EE is **49.363563% below UNILATERAL**, while ORACLE_SET is
+**6.359000% above UNILATERAL**. Therefore
+
+\[
+\frac{EE_{FLOOR}-EE_{UNILATERAL}}
+     {EE_{ORACLE\_SET}-EE_{UNILATERAL}}
+=\frac{14{,}416{,}651.408-28{,}470{,}904.273}
+       {30{,}281{,}369.063-28{,}470{,}904.273}
+=\mathbf{-7.7627871789}.
+\]
+
+This is a clear negative result. The invariant removes the targeted
+occupancy-1/2 regime and greatly improves the incumbent, but it does not
+recover post-unilateral coordination headroom. It also serves fewer users
+than UNILATERAL at every anchor, so no apparent gain could be credited on the
+requested service criterion.
+
+## Pooled endpoint
+
+Pooled EE is the ratio of summed decoded bits to summed corrected-engine
+joules, not the mean of per-anchor ratios.
+
+| Arm | Decoded bits | Joules | Pooled EE (bit/J) | Served count |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| BASELINE | 545,927,267,996.825 | 146,564.590466 | **3,724,823.753560** | 826 |
+| UNILATERAL | 1,660,779,577,104.985 | 58,332.519445 | **28,470,904.272641** | 1,939 |
+| FLOOR | 1,057,317,963,467.053 | 73,340.051969 | **14,416,651.407803** | 1,450 |
+| ORACLE_SET | 1,694,404,970,756.872 | 55,955.362098 | **30,281,369.063314** | 1,957 |
+
+FLOOR versus BASELINE is **+287.042512% EE**: decoded bits rise 93.6738%,
+energy falls 49.9606%, and served count rises from 826 to 1,450. FLOOR beats
+BASELINE in EE and serves at least as many users on all 20 anchors.
+
+FLOOR versus UNILATERAL is **−49.363563% EE**: decoded bits fall 36.3360%,
+energy rises 25.7276%, and served count falls by 489 (25.2192%). It serves at
+least as many users as UNILATERAL on **0/20 anchors**. ORACLE_SET's reference
+gain over UNILATERAL is **+6.359000%**.
+
+## Fixed policy actually run
+
+FLOOR starts directly from **BASELINE**, the incumbent `nearest-eligible`
+assignment. It does not start from UNILATERAL.
+
+1. Record the initially active beams with occupancy one or two and visit that
+   fixed list once in ascending `(satellite, beam)` identity order.
+2. At each still-underfull beam, prescribe at most two complete repairs:
+   consolidation imports the nearest-slant legal occupants of other currently
+   underfull beams until occupancy three; evacuation moves every occupant to
+   its nearest-slant legal beam already at occupancy at least three. A user is
+   assigned `NULL` only when no such evacuation destination is legal.
+3. Score those prescribed branches at realised boundary 0 with the unchanged
+   exact binary64 objective
+   `F = bits − 19,720,681.00172232 × joules`. A branch remains eligible only
+   when its served count is at least BASELINE's unchanged boundary-0 service
+   guard. Choose greater exact F; ties prefer greater service, consolidation,
+   then lexicographically smaller configuration identity.
+4. Commit immediately and continue the one pass. There is no no-op branch:
+   the invariant is mandatory. The committed assignment is then evaluated on
+   the same complete 48-boundary realised endpoint as the other arms.
+
+This is a whole-assignment policy, not the prior three-family per-anchor rule
+coordinator. Only threshold **3** was tried. No threshold, sign, seed, horizon,
+price, service guard, or acceptance rule was varied after outcomes were seen.
+
+## Occupancy result
+
+Across the 20 anchors, 503 of 835 initially active beam incidences were below
+the floor: **60.2395%**. The one pass left no active beam below occupancy three.
+
+| Occupancy | Active beams before | Active beams after |
+|---:|---:|---:|
+| 1 | 262 | 0 |
+| 2 | 241 | 0 |
+| 3 | 151 | 70 |
+| 4 | 127 | 84 |
+| 5 | 39 | 88 |
+| 6 | 5 | 42 |
+| 7 | 10 | 49 |
+| 8 | 0 | 23 |
+| 9 | 0 | 2 |
+| 10 | 0 | 2 |
+| 11 | 0 | 2 |
+| **Total active** | **835** | **362** |
+
+Of the 503 initially underfull beams, **30 were consolidated** to occupancy at
+least three and **473 were emptied**. There were 470 explicit repair decisions
+(30 consolidate, 440 empty); another 33 beams emptied indirectly when their
+occupants were used as consolidation donors. The policy changed 702 user
+assignments in total. Across committed FLOOR assignments, 175 user-anchor
+incidences ended at `NULL` because no already-stable legal evacuation beam was
+available.
+
+## Every anchor, including service and failure mechanism
+
+EE columns are million bit/J. `Served B/U/F/O` gives BASELINE, UNILATERAL,
+FLOOR, and ORACLE_SET. `Δbits` and `ΔJ` are FLOOR relative to UNILATERAL;
+`C/E` counts initially underfull beams consolidated/emptied. These deltas state
+why FLOOR is worse at each anchor.
+
+| Anchor | B EE | U EE | F EE | O EE | Served B/U/F/O | F vs U EE | Δbits | ΔJ | C/E | Users moved | Decision s |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| W1/A0 | 4.081 | 31.359 | 14.750 | 32.863 | 43/98/70/99 | −52.96% | −39.6% | +28.3% | 4/24 | 35 | 38.433 |
+| W1/A1 | 3.760 | 35.290 | 17.055 | 37.286 | 37/99/73/99 | −51.67% | −37.4% | +29.6% | 1/26 | 40 | 34.707 |
+| W1/A2 | 4.785 | 24.594 | 16.558 | 28.025 | 40/97/72/98 | −32.68% | −32.5% | +0.3% | 2/22 | 33 | 23.201 |
+| W1/A3 | 3.128 | 19.727 | 14.383 | 23.168 | 35/90/68/99 | −27.09% | −28.7% | −2.2% | 2/24 | 33 | 31.525 |
+| W1/A4 | 4.149 | 36.183 | 11.456 | 36.490 | 43/99/65/99 | −68.34% | −44.9% | +74.0% | 2/19 | 26 | 21.756 |
+| W2/A0 | 3.075 | 31.565 | 14.485 | 32.275 | 33/99/68/99 | −54.11% | −41.1% | +28.4% | 0/23 | 35 | 26.030 |
+| W2/A1 | 4.914 | 39.257 | 15.134 | 40.548 | 44/98/69/98 | −61.45% | −38.0% | +60.9% | 0/23 | 35 | 23.436 |
+| W2/A2 | 5.187 | 30.489 | 18.326 | 31.183 | 45/100/76/100 | −39.89% | −31.6% | +13.7% | 0/23 | 35 | 23.026 |
+| W2/A3 | 2.662 | 16.474 | 14.538 | 17.002 | 36/98/71/98 | −11.75% | −29.9% | −20.6% | 0/23 | 35 | 27.005 |
+| W2/A4 | 6.229 | 26.729 | 16.440 | 30.811 | 58/97/72/98 | −38.49% | −32.7% | +9.4% | 0/25 | 34 | 30.251 |
+| W3/A0 | 3.455 | 28.234 | 13.544 | 29.611 | 43/96/74/96 | −52.03% | −36.4% | +32.5% | 2/25 | 40 | 28.168 |
+| W3/A1 | 4.075 | 33.196 | 15.865 | 35.549 | 43/98/77/99 | −52.21% | −35.4% | +35.2% | 1/25 | 36 | 30.455 |
+| W3/A2 | 5.708 | 25.950 | 18.596 | 26.602 | 50/96/86/97 | −28.34% | −23.3% | +7.1% | 1/25 | 36 | 31.265 |
+| W3/A3 | 3.128 | 22.713 | 14.124 | 25.213 | 42/93/78/95 | −37.81% | −33.8% | +6.4% | 1/25 | 36 | 29.456 |
+| W3/A4 | 1.948 | 34.659 | 8.444 | 37.127 | 28/91/55/93 | −75.64% | −59.2% | +67.4% | 0/25 | 40 | 26.984 |
+| W4/A0 | 2.748 | 35.208 | 11.525 | 35.852 | 33/97/71/97 | −67.27% | −42.7% | +75.1% | 2/25 | 37 | 38.683 |
+| W4/A1 | 3.867 | 32.704 | 14.790 | 34.377 | 47/97/81/97 | −54.77% | −30.0% | +54.8% | 3/23 | 34 | 28.719 |
+| W4/A2 | 4.762 | 32.020 | 16.942 | 34.013 | 53/99/82/99 | −47.09% | −27.4% | +37.3% | 3/23 | 34 | 29.618 |
+| W4/A3 | 2.259 | 24.747 | 13.057 | 27.023 | 39/100/76/100 | −47.24% | −35.5% | +22.2% | 3/23 | 34 | 31.969 |
+| W4/A4 | 2.619 | 33.251 | 10.416 | 34.010 | 34/97/66/97 | −68.68% | −50.1% | +59.3% | 3/22 | 34 | 27.641 |
+
+FLOOR is worse than UNILATERAL on **all 20 anchors** and worse than BASELINE
+on **none**. All 20 lose decoded bits relative to UNILATERAL. Eighteen also use
+more energy; W1/A3 and W2/A3 use less energy, but their 28.7% and 29.9% bit
+losses dominate. All 20 serve fewer users than UNILATERAL.
+
+The causal explanation visible in the measurements is that occupancy three is
+necessary for the first credited mode in the stated regime, but it is not
+sufficient for an efficient complete assignment. The floor collapses active
+beams from 835 to 362 and eliminates the zero-mode occupancy class, yet its
+nearest-slant evacuations strand 175 user-anchor incidences and do not perform
+UNILATERAL's user-specific power/interference reassignment. The mandatory
+one-pass commits can also accept the less damaging of two repairs even when
+both are worse than the current partial assignment. The result is much better
+than the sparse incumbent, but simultaneously fewer bits and usually more
+energy than the coordinate-wise optimum.
+
+## Decision time
+
+The measured FLOOR decision includes construction and exact boundary-0
+scoring of both prescribed branches at each visited beam:
+
+- mean **29.116360 s**; p50 **29.087240 s**; p95 **38.445949 s**; maximum
+  **38.682846 s**; total **582.327209 s** over 20 anchors;
+- 8/20 decisions exceed the engine's 30.08-s snapshot interval;
+- the non-simulator rule bookkeeping alone averaged **16.733 ms** (p95
+  23.456 ms, max 25.504 ms), but that is not the decision time because the
+  branch rule was explicitly defined by exact F;
+- 26,140 exact physical boundary evaluations were charged during FLOOR branch
+  scoring.
+
+This is not a sub-millisecond deployable result. The complete diagnostic took
+820.904 s (13 min 40.904 s) in one `nice -n 12` process with one thread per
+numeric library, within the requested maximum of three processes.
+
+## Panel, evaluator, and integrity
+
+- Same real ceiling panel: four `V025_PROBE_R2` TRAIN worlds × first five
+  decision anchors = 20 anchors. The world digests and seeds match the ceiling
+  receipt. No TEST or claim-panel world was opened.
+- BASELINE, the certified no-deadline UNILATERAL local optimum, and ORACLE_SET
+  were reconstructed from the authenticated ceiling receipt and re-evaluated
+  alongside FLOOR with the current exact 48-boundary evaluator. Their
+  configuration identities, served counts, bits, and joules reproduced (the
+  largest replay difference was at floating-point roundoff scale).
+- Corrected physics source: requested engine commit `75c5c78c`; source tree
+  `1728f6b0462f86d85618a4c73f4d1dd2d2c07376`; local starting commit
+  `06f4b1c`; probe SHA-256
+  `f4122d6784cb56de7743c55d51dc80a6c968ccea601d637cd1b41a8b5604c76c`.
+- Oracle input file SHA-256:
+  `af5a0ae34fd511b1598ab79d004be311fb1f1ea2478ca276ecbe3e8c96c79a83`;
+  authenticated embedded receipt:
+  `07c120297370f2b1a4826fce723950bccaf9e1a4e81007cda4ae30fae975fc29`.
+- FLOOR result file SHA-256:
+  `0991cfecf880e01cd5fe1e1a89ee07333ffdb9e4d6a618883f260f7147002ed4`;
+  authenticated embedded receipt:
+  `34e1034997b54b9670be96716ccbd34b42d0ede0e8a98cd402af0a4ae0dd4eba`.
+- The independent verifier reaggregated every arm, recomputed the captured
+  fraction, checked every occupancy histogram and repair count, validated the
+  receipt hash and process/threshold declarations, and returned `VERIFIED`.
+  Three focused policy tests also pass.
+
+Reproducible local artifacts:
+
+- [policy implementation](src/mcrl/physics_v025/occupancy_floor.py)
+- [diagnostic runner](.scratch/occupancy-floor/run_occupancy_floor.py)
+- [raw 20-anchor receipt](.scratch/occupancy-floor/occupancy-floor-result.json)
+- [independent verifier](.scratch/occupancy-floor/verify_occupancy_floor_result.py)
+
+## Bottom line
+
+The occupancy floor captures **little in the strongest possible sense: its
+captured fraction is negative**. It exposes a large, real incumbent
+inefficiency, but it does not explain the oracle's gain over exhaustive
+unilateral optimisation. On this panel, eliminating occupancy-one/two beams
+is not the missing coordination mechanism; the residual structure is
+genuinely non-trivial and includes which users move where, service retention,
+and joint power/interference effects.
diff --git a/src/mcrl/physics_v025/occupancy_floor.py b/src/mcrl/physics_v025/occupancy_floor.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..e6fbcd609824c820fcc4544102b92360ea71e5b4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/mcrl/physics_v025/occupancy_floor.py
@@ -0,0 +1,243 @@
+"""Deterministic one-pass occupancy-three floor policy.
+
+The policy repairs the incumbent assignment directly.  It is not a candidate
+catalogue: each underfull beam has at most two prescribed repairs, and a
+caller-provided exact scorer chooses between those repairs.
+"""
+
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+from collections import Counter
+from dataclasses import dataclass
+from fractions import Fraction
+from typing import Callable, Mapping, Sequence
+
+
+BeamIdentity = tuple[int, int]
+Assignment = BeamIdentity | None
+MIN_OCCUPANCY = 3
+
+
+@dataclass(frozen=True)
+class RepairPlan:
+    """One prescribed repair for the beam currently being visited."""
+
+    action: str
+    beam: BeamIdentity
+    assignments: tuple[tuple[int, Assignment], ...]
+    moved_users: tuple[int, ...]
+
+    @property
+    def mapping(self) -> dict[int, Assignment]:
+        return dict(self.assignments)
+
+
+@dataclass(frozen=True)
+class ScoredRepair:
+    """The exact decision-boundary score used by the branch rule."""
+
+    plan: RepairPlan
+    objective: Fraction
+    served_count: int
+    configuration_id: str
+
+
+@dataclass(frozen=True)
+class FloorResult:
+    """Committed output and audit trail of the single policy pass."""
+
+    assignments: tuple[tuple[int, Assignment], ...]
+    decisions: tuple[ScoredRepair, ...]
+    initially_underfull: tuple[BeamIdentity, ...]
+
+    @property
+    def mapping(self) -> dict[int, Assignment]:
+        return dict(self.assignments)
+
+
+def occupancies(assignments: Mapping[int, Assignment]) -> Counter[BeamIdentity]:
+    """Return active-beam occupancies; empty and NULL beams are absent."""
+
+    return Counter(beam for beam in assignments.values() if beam is not None)
+
+
+def occupancy_histogram(assignments: Mapping[int, Assignment]) -> dict[int, int]:
+    """Map occupancy to the number of active beams at that occupancy."""
+
+    return dict(sorted(Counter(occupancies(assignments).values()).items()))
+
+
+def _empty_plan(
+    current: Mapping[int, Assignment],
+    *,
+    beam: BeamIdentity,
+    legal_options: Mapping[int, Sequence[BeamIdentity]],
+    slant_km: Mapping[tuple[int, BeamIdentity], float],
+) -> RepairPlan:
+    """Evacuate every occupant to its nearest already-stable legal beam."""
+
+    counts = occupancies(current)
+    occupants = tuple(sorted(user for user, value in current.items() if value == beam))
+    mapping = dict(current)
+    for user in occupants:
+        destinations = tuple(
+            candidate
+            for candidate in legal_options.get(user, ())
+            if candidate != beam and counts.get(candidate, 0) >= MIN_OCCUPANCY
+        )
+        mapping[user] = min(
+            destinations,
+            key=lambda candidate: (slant_km[(user, candidate)], candidate),
+            default=None,
+        )
+    return RepairPlan(
+        action="empty",
+        beam=beam,
+        assignments=tuple(sorted(mapping.items())),
+        moved_users=occupants,
+    )
+
+
+def _consolidate_plan(
+    current: Mapping[int, Assignment],
+    *,
+    beam: BeamIdentity,
+    legal_options: Mapping[int, Sequence[BeamIdentity]],
+    slant_km: Mapping[tuple[int, BeamIdentity], float],
+) -> RepairPlan | None:
+    """Fill a beam from other underfull beams using nearest-link order."""
+
+    counts = occupancies(current)
+    needed = MIN_OCCUPANCY - counts.get(beam, 0)
+    if needed <= 0:
+        return None
+    arrivals = sorted(
+        (
+            slant_km[(user, beam)],
+            user,
+            origin,
+        )
+        for user, origin in current.items()
+        if origin is not None
+        and origin != beam
+        and counts.get(origin, 0) < MIN_OCCUPANCY
+        and beam in legal_options.get(user, ())
+        and (user, beam) in slant_km
+    )
+    if len(arrivals) < needed:
+        return None
+    moved = tuple(user for _slant, user, _origin in arrivals[:needed])
+    mapping = dict(current)
+    for user in moved:
+        mapping[user] = beam
+    return RepairPlan(
+        action="consolidate",
+        beam=beam,
+        assignments=tuple(sorted(mapping.items())),
+        moved_users=moved,
+    )
+
+
+def repair_plans(
+    current: Mapping[int, Assignment],
+    *,
+    beam: BeamIdentity,
+    legal_options: Mapping[int, Sequence[BeamIdentity]],
+    slant_km: Mapping[tuple[int, BeamIdentity], float],
+) -> tuple[RepairPlan, ...]:
+    """Return the two fixed branches, or only evacuation when filling is impossible."""
+
+    consolidate = _consolidate_plan(
+        current,
+        beam=beam,
+        legal_options=legal_options,
+        slant_km=slant_km,
+    )
+    empty = _empty_plan(
+        current,
+        beam=beam,
+        legal_options=legal_options,
+        slant_km=slant_km,
+    )
+    return (empty,) if consolidate is None else (consolidate, empty)
+
+
+def apply_occupancy_floor(
+    assignments: Mapping[int, Assignment],
+    *,
+    legal_options: Mapping[int, Sequence[BeamIdentity]],
+    slant_km: Mapping[tuple[int, BeamIdentity], float],
+    exact_score: Callable[[RepairPlan], ScoredRepair | None],
+    minimum_served: int,
+) -> FloorResult:
+    """Apply one sorted pass and commit the best service-safe exact repair.
+
+    Branch order is objective descending, served count descending, action
+    (``consolidate`` before ``empty``), then configuration id.  A branch that
+    is physically invalid or below the unchanged service guard is ineligible.
+    """
+
+    current = dict(assignments)
+    initial_counts = occupancies(current)
+    initially_underfull = tuple(
+        beam
+        for beam, count in sorted(initial_counts.items())
+        if 0 < count < MIN_OCCUPANCY
+    )
+    decisions: list[ScoredRepair] = []
+    action_rank = {"consolidate": 0, "empty": 1}
+    for beam in initially_underfull:
+        count = occupancies(current).get(beam, 0)
+        if count == 0 or count >= MIN_OCCUPANCY:
+            continue
+        scored = tuple(
+            row
+            for plan in repair_plans(
+                current,
+                beam=beam,
+                legal_options=legal_options,
+                slant_km=slant_km,
+            )
+            if (row := exact_score(plan)) is not None
+            and row.served_count >= minimum_served
+        )
+        if not scored:
+            raise RuntimeError(f"no service-safe occupancy-floor repair for beam {beam}")
+        selected = min(
+            scored,
+            key=lambda row: (
+                -row.objective,
+                -row.served_count,
+                action_rank[row.plan.action],
+                row.configuration_id,
+            ),
+        )
+        current = selected.plan.mapping
+        decisions.append(selected)
+
+    residual = {
+        beam: count
+        for beam, count in occupancies(current).items()
+        if count < MIN_OCCUPANCY
+    }
+    if residual:
+        raise RuntimeError(f"occupancy-floor invariant was not established: {residual}")
+    return FloorResult(
+        assignments=tuple(sorted(current.items())),
+        decisions=tuple(decisions),
+        initially_underfull=initially_underfull,
+    )
+
+
+__all__ = [
+    "Assignment",
+    "BeamIdentity",
+    "FloorResult",
+    "MIN_OCCUPANCY",
+    "RepairPlan",
+    "ScoredRepair",
+    "apply_occupancy_floor",
+    "occupancies",
+    "occupancy_histogram",
+    "repair_plans",
+]
